Everything in this directory is the data product:

    scoreboard.db              the Scoreboard, SQLite
    csv_tables/*.csv           flat exports of every table, including the
                               audit trail

It is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License. Use it for anything, commercial work included. The one condition is
attribution: when you publish a figure or a number drawn from these rows, name
the Scoreboard. This satisfies it:

    The Promised vs. Produced Scoreboard, IndustriousAF. CC BY 4.0.
    https://github.com/ashwinl4/promised-vs-produced-scoreboard

    Deed         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Legal code   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode


This file exists because these CSVs travel. They get copied into an analysis
folder, mailed as an attachment, dropped into a notebook — and arrive with no
README anywhere near them. So the notice lives beside the data too.

The code that produced these files is licensed MIT, not CC BY. That is a
different license covering different files; see LICENSE in the repository root.
Full data terms, including what is not covered, are in LICENSE-DATA there.
